{pad:meta title='Notations'/}
<p class="nt-lead">Text written in a notation and drawn on the server - a formula, a chemical equation,
a tune, a chord, a word in braille, morse or flags, a chess, go or draughts position, a guitar tab, a Karnaugh map, a bridge deal, a juggling pattern, the moves of a cube. Each is a
tag of its own, a file of <code>pad/subs/notations/types/</code> in the engine, written <code>{pad:open/}notation:kind 'text'/{pad:close/}</code>. The text is its
first parameter or the content between its tags. What comes out is MathML, HTML or inline SVG -
no script, the same for the same text, and readable by a screen reader.</p>

<ul class="nt-cards">
  {array:notations}
  <li><a class="nt-card" href="?{$kind}"><b>{$name}</b><span>{$line}</span><code>{$tag}</code></a></li>
  {/array:notations}
</ul>
